		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3514&amp;p=28760#p28760"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I noticed there's a new CSV feature called "Update location from CSV" but I can't seem to find any documentation on how this works. Do I just need to chill until the new feature is finished or is my Google-fu failing me and I'm just not seeing the note that explains how it works?</div></blockquote>Documentation is not up to date, and actually the CPS does not have a User Guide<br><br>Information about this was probably posted when it was added to the CPS, but this function opens a CSV file which must have 3 columns<br><br>Channel Name,Lat,Lon<br><br>The Channel Name must match the name you assigned to the channel<br><br>i.e if your channels e.g. repeaters are named with the callsign of the repeater, then its possible to download the Repeater Book data containing the Lat/Lon position, then reformatting the spreadsheet to remove the other columns<br><br>However it only works if you name the Channel with the callsign or some other information which you can crossreference from Repeater Book or other sources<br><br>Personally I used the repeater callsigns for the channel names, but I know many people have their own system of naming, e.g. the town/city or perhaps mountain location, in which case this won't work unless you can build a spreadsheet which has names which match your channel names<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Jan 18, 2024 9:01 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
